  "facts": [
    "Merged vf-run adds a real in-process RunnerConfig -> load_environment -> selected bounded taskset -> env.serving -> env.slots/run_slot -> on_complete/append_episode path. The integration run fixture and example CLI smoke calls now use it.",
    "Every slot is scheduled eagerly with ensure_future and all returned episodes are retained by gather. max_concurrent defaults to128; Env.run_slot holds that semaphore per attempt, releases it before retry backoff and before persistence. This bounds active episode attempts, not the queued task list, retained histories, total model calls, tokens or scoring spend.",
    "An exception from a rollout/taskset or another BaseException path cancels siblings and awaits their unwind before serving teardown. on_complete stamps EvalRunInfo on the episode and its traces; append_episode shields lock acquisition and its worker write against ordinary cancellation. An ordinary Episode(ok=False) is gathered with its siblings and causes the CLI nonzero exit only at summary; it is distinct from a raised exception.",
    "The CLI and direct run_episodes reject an existing nonempty traces.jsonl. There is no resume implementation. save_config starts an empty trace file for a fresh run; write_episode uses an append file write without an fsync call in this reviewed path.",
    "The summary reports episode.ok counts but averages Trace.reward across every trace, including all seats in multi-agent episodes. Trace.reward sums non-None reward values; this summary does not separately count scored, skipped, dropped or training-admitted traces.",
    "Immediately subsequent landed PR2610 removes vf-eval at1bcdb8baeda8638125db5678c9d54d26a35cb64e, and its immediate child PR3052 removes vf-replay at2310f5d2aea89781b05815dc1b4a032417788859. Exact pyproject entries shrink6->5->4; docs direct short runs to vf-run, full evaluation to prime-rl uv run eval and saved-trace rescoring to library Task.rescore guidance. Earlier CLI/resume evidence stays historical and pinned."
  ],
  "our_inference": "vf-run supplies a concrete smaller integration target for future runner-bound H3/H4 budget/version work. Its active-attempt semaphore, persistence hook and cancellation unwind must be evaluated separately from durable global budgets, recovery, score membership and general scale behavior. This identifies a caller, not an accepted integration or a preregistered experiment.",
  "author_test_claims": "PR3047 reports unit tests, selected integrations and22 live Prime Inference checks. We read the new unit-test designs, whose failure/cancellation controls use FakeEnv and an artificial Taskset; we did not execute them or reproduce the live checks.",
  "scientific_experiments": 0,
  "native_suites": 0,
  "local_tests": 0,
  "model_loads": 0,
  "limits": "Source and author-test-design review only: no package installation, local upstream tests, native/model/provider/cloud execution, scientific suite, resource benchmark or crash/restart validation. Author-reported live inference checks are not our measurements. No complete dependency closure or system-call durability audit. Existing H1/H2 accepted and failed evidence, finite closed gates, and H3/H4 scientific statuses remain unchanged.",
